>> title: Croissant Dough
>> category: Pastry & Doughs
>> tags: pastry, laminated, yeast, butter, make-ahead
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: pâte à croissant, pate a croissant, croissant dough, viennoiserie dough, yeasted laminated dough, yeasted puff pastry
>> pairs-with: croissant, pain-au-chocolat
>> servings: 12
>> time: 14 hr
>> slack: unforgiving — butter colder than the dough shatters into shards and warmer smears into it, and either way the layers are gone for good

>> step: mix to a smooth dough, chill overnight
Mix @bread flour{3 3/4%cup}(500 g), @cold whole milk{1 1/4%cup}(300 mL), @granulated sugar{1/4%cup}(55 g), @instant yeast{2 1/4%tsp}(7 g), @table salt{2%tsp}(11 g) and @softened unsalted butter{3%Tbs}(40 g) to a smooth dough, knead it four minutes only, flatten it into a rectangle and ~chill{10%hr} overnight.

>> step: beat the block to a square, chill 20 min
Beat @cold unsalted butter{1 1/8%cup}(250 g) between two sheets of paper into a 7-inch square, then ~firm{20%min} in the #refrigerator{}.

>> step: fold the dough round the block and roll it long
Roll @&(~2)chilled dough{} to a 10-by-14-inch rectangle, lay @&(~1)butter block{} on one half, fold the bare half over and pinch it shut, then roll it out to three times its width.

>> step: fold in three, turn, chill 45 min — three times
Fold @&(~1)parcel{} in three like a letter, turn it a quarter, roll it long again and ~chill{45%min} — three times in all.

>> step: rest 1 hour before it is cut
Rest @&(~1)laminated dough{}, wrapped, in the #refrigerator{} ~rest{1%hr} before it is cut.
